# Deploying {{ project_name }} to {{ {"aws": "AWS", "azure": "Azure", "gcp": "Google Cloud"}[cloud] }}

Generated from the project spec. Everything here is code you can read and change: GitHub Actions workflows
in `.github/workflows/` and Terraform in `deploy/{{ cloud }}/`. **No cloud credential is stored anywhere**:
the pipeline signs in with a short-lived OIDC token that GitHub issues per run, and the cloud only accepts
tokens from this repository (`{{ repo }}`) and, for deployments, from a named GitHub environment.

## What you get

| Piece | Where | Does |
|---|---|---|
| CI | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | lint, tests against PostgreSQL, `alembic check`, image build, vulnerability scan (fails on a fixable HIGH or CRITICAL), SBOM, `terraform fmt` and `validate` |
| CD | `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` | push to `main` deploys **{{ environments[0] }}**; "Run workflow" promotes a tag to any environment: build once, push, sign, migrate, deploy, smoke test |
| Stack | `deploy/{{ cloud }}/` | private network, private database, secret manager, service, load balancing |
| One-time setup | `deploy/{{ cloud }}/bootstrap/` | state storage, image registry, the OIDC trust (run by an administrator, once) |
| Capacity | `deploy/{{ cloud }}/environments/*.tfvars` | numbers per environment: instances, CPU, memory, database size |

{% if cloud == "aws" %}
Runs on **ECS Fargate** behind an **Application Load Balancer** (with AWS WAF), **RDS for PostgreSQL** in
private subnets, secrets in **Secrets Manager**, images in **ECR**. A NAT gateway gives the private subnets
outbound access: it is billed by the hour and is the largest fixed cost of a small environment.
{% elif cloud == "azure" %}
Runs on **Azure Container Apps** with a managed HTTPS address, **PostgreSQL Flexible Server** on a private
network, secrets in **Key Vault**, images in **Container Registry**. There is no web application firewall in
this bundle (Front Door adds one).
{% else %}
Runs on **Cloud Run** with a managed HTTPS address, **Cloud SQL** with a private IP, secrets in **Secret
Manager**, images in **Artifact Registry**. There is no web application firewall in this bundle (Cloud Armor
needs a load balancer in front).
{% endif %}

## One-time setup (about 20 minutes)

1. **Create the identities and storage.** In `deploy/{{ cloud }}/bootstrap/`, sign in with your own
{% if cloud == "aws" %}
   AWS credentials and run `terraform init && terraform apply`. Review the plan first: it creates an S3 state
   bucket, an ECR repository, the GitHub OIDC provider (set `create_oidc_provider = false` if your account
   already has one) and one deploy role per environment.
{% elif cloud == "azure" %}
   account (`az login`; you need rights to create applications in Entra ID and to assign roles) and run
   `terraform init && terraform apply -var subscription_id=<id>`. It creates a state storage account (no account
   keys), a container registry, and one Entra application per environment with a federated credential.
{% else %}
   account (`gcloud auth application-default login`) and run
   `terraform init && terraform apply -var project_id=<your project id>`. It creates a state bucket, an
   Artifact Registry repository, a Workload Identity pool and one service account per environment.
{% endif %}
   Keep the `terraform.tfstate` it leaves in that folder somewhere safe: it is the only record of these.
2. **Create the GitHub environments** (Settings > Environments): {% for e in environments %}`{{ e }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
   On the production environment add **required reviewers** (and restrict it to the `main` branch). The trust
   in step 1 is per environment, so nobody can deploy to production without passing through it.
3. **Set the variables** of each GitHub environment (not secrets: none of these is secret) from the
   bootstrap's outputs:

{% if cloud == "aws" %}
   | Variable | Value |
   |---|---|
   | `AWS_ROLE_ARN` | the role for this environment (`deploy_role_arns`) |
   | `AWS_REGION` | `{{ region }}` |
   | `TF_STATE_BUCKET` | `state_bucket` |
   | `ECR_REPOSITORY_URL` | `ecr_repository_url` |
{% elif cloud == "azure" %}
   | Variable | Value |
   |---|---|
   | `AZURE_CLIENT_ID` | the application for this environment (`deploy_client_ids`) |
   | `AZURE_TENANT_ID` | `tenant_id` |
   | `AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID` | your subscription id |
   | `ACR_NAME` | `registry_name` |
   | `TF_STATE_RESOURCE_GROUP` | `state_resource_group` |
   | `TF_STATE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT` | `state_storage_account` |
{% else %}
   | Variable | Value |
   |---|---|
   | `GCP_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_PROVIDER` | `workload_identity_provider` |
   | `GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT` | the account for this environment (`deploy_service_accounts`) |
   | `GCP_PROJECT_ID` | your project id |
   | `GCP_REGION` | `{{ region }}` |
   | `TF_STATE_BUCKET` | `state_bucket` |
   | `GCP_REGISTRY` | `registry` |
{% endif %}
